    "update_time": 1785467917.7799127,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "In Virginia, briefly:\n- Sign the title over to the buyer (seller section, odometer reading), and give a bill of sale (DMV form SUR 1 or a simple written one).\n- **Remove your plates.** In VA plates stay with the seller; return them to DMV or transfer them, and cancel insurance after the sale, not before.\n- Notify DMV of the sale (online \"Notice of Sale\"), which protects you from tolls and tickets after the handover.\n- Accept payment in cash or a cashier's check verified at the bank; avoid personal checks and payment apps for the full amount."
     ]
    },
